The generator uses the reference implementations of half-aggregation and full-aggregation in [[bip_cisa_psbt/halfagg.py|halfagg.py]] and [[bip_cisa_psbt/fullagg.py|fullagg.py]], which are licensed under the same terms.

=== Motivation ===

BIP 460 introduces witness version 2 outputs whose key path spends can be aggregated across the inputs of a transaction.
A signer of such an input no longer produces the final witness by itself.
For half-aggregation as specified in [[bip-0458.mediawiki|BIP 458]], the final witness of a group can only be built once the individual signatures of all inputs in the group are available.
For full-aggregation as specified in [[bip-0459.mediawiki|BIP 459]], the signers also have to exchange nonces before they can sign.
PSBT is the standard format for passing a transaction between signers and other participants.
It therefore needs fields for the aggregation mode and for the signature material of both schemes, and rules for when an aggregated input can be finalized.

== Specification ==

The fields of [[bip-0371.mediawiki|BIP 371]] apply to witness version 2 inputs and outputs exactly as to Taproot inputs and outputs, including <tt>PSBT_IN_TAP_KEY_SIG</tt> for the signature of an opted-out key path spend.

The new per-input types are defined as follows:

